            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LIN01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Theophilus</forename>
                        <surname>Lindsey</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1723-06-20">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1808-11-03"/>
                    <occupation>Unitarian minister</occupation>
                    <occupation>theologian</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Eminent dissenting theologian and minister. Lindsey operated from a chapel in Essex St, London which hosted the first Unitarian congregation 
      when it opened in 1778. Lindsey was an associate of <persName key="PRI01">Joseph Priestley</persName>, <persName key="PRI02">Richard Price</persName>, 
      and<persName key="DIS01"> John Disney</persName> and was involved in the movement to repeal the
      Test and Corporation Acts in the late 1780s and early 1790s.</p>
                        <p>Lindsey was married thus the 'H Lindsey' that Godwin refers to in 1809 may be his widow Hannah (nee Elsworth) (1740–1812).</p>
                        <p>Lindsey is not to be confused with Lindsay which refers to <persName key="LIN03">James Lindsay</persName>, also a dissenting minister recorded in the diary.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
